      <section class="editorial-chapter">
        <h2>House Rent Allowance (HRA) Classification in Uttar Pradesh</h2>
        <p>
          In Uttar Pradesh, House Rent Allowance is categorized based on population density under state financial rules (Financial Handbook Volume V):
        </p>

        <div class="city-classification-grid">
          <div class="city-box tier-a">
            <h4>Class A (Metropolitan & NCR Cities)</h4>
            <div class="badge-tag">Population 50 Lakh+ / NCR Region</div>
            <p><strong>Baseline HRA Rate:</strong> 27% of Basic Pay (Projected up to 30%).</p>
            <p><strong>Covered Cities:</strong> Noida, Greater Noida, Ghaziabad, Lucknow Corporation Limits, and Kanpur Nagar.</p>
            <span class="card-footer-note">Highest urban rental cost tier in the state.</span>
          </div>

          <div class="city-box tier-b">
