        </p>
        <ul class="bullet-feature-list">
          <li><strong>The NPS Landscape:</strong> State employees joining regular service after April 1, 2005 are enrolled under the National Pension System (NPS), contributing 10% of their Basic Pay &plus; DA, with matching state contributions. Employee federations continue active campaigns advocating for the restoration of the defined-benefit <strong>Old Pension Scheme (OPS)</strong> or adoption of the <strong>Unified Pension Scheme (UPS)</strong> model.</li>
          <li><strong>Revision for Existing Pensioners:</strong> Over twelve lakh retired state employees and family pensioners will see their baseline monthly pension multiplied directly by the finalized fitment factor. The statutory minimum pension in UP will rise from ₹9,000 to approximately <strong>₹20,520 per month</strong> under the 2.28 factor.</li>
          <li><strong>State Health Scheme Integration:</strong> Pensioners benefit from the Pandit Deendayal Upadhyaya Rajya Karamchari Cashless Chikitsa Yojana (SECHS), providing cashless hospitalization coverage alongside revised pension disbursements.</li>
